      "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7520902740739297281/",
      "text": "Hiring isn't an HR task. It’s your core growth driver. Every new team member either raises your operational standard or lowers it. There is no middle ground. A brilliant strategy means nothing without the right operators to execute it. If you want high-performing teams, stop rushing the recruitment process. Focus on: 1.) Knowing exactly what capability you need 2.) Screening for character and grit over a slick CV 3.) Being radically transparent about the reality of the role Building a world-class team means setting people up to win. That requires clear direction, real autonomy, and ongoing support. Hiring strong people and leaving them to sink or swim without adequate support. It doesn't work, and that is on us as leaders. If you expect big results from your people, you owe them the tools and clarity to deliver. #Recruitment #Leadership #Hiring #BusinessGrowth … more",
