      "text": "72% of open roles added in India this quarter are concentrated in sectors that most job seekers haven't even updated their profiles for yet. That gap is expensive. Here's where the real momentum is building right now: → Climate tech & renewable infrastructure (hiring up sharply as ESG mandates kick in) → Healthcare SaaS & diagnostics platforms (post-pandemic digitisation isn't slowing) → Regional language content & vernacular media (brands finally chasing Tier 2 & 3 audiences) → Supply chain tech (global disruptions have made this a boardroom priority) None of these are niche anymore. They're mainstream — and they're hiring people who've positioned themselves correctly, not just people who've applied the most. The question worth sitting with today: does your profile speak the language of where hiring is actually going? If you're not sure, start there. 👇 #HiringTrends #IndianJobMarket #CareerGrowth #JobSearchIndia #KindJobs #JobTips #LinkedInIndia … more",
