      "id": "LI00256",
      "sourceId": "LI00256",
      "url": null,
      "text": "\"Employers have all the leverage right now.\" I hear this almost every day. And while that may be true in many markets, Orlando feels different. The Orlando metro added more than 20,000 jobs over the last year, leading the state in job growth and outperforming Florida's other major metros. Yet many of the hiring leaders I speak with are telling the same story: finding exceptional talent is still difficult. There are more applicants. There are not necessarily more qualified applicants. The companies winning in Orlando aren't assuming the market will do the work for them. They're investing in their employer brand, moving quickly, and treating recruiting like a competitive advantage. Because even in a market that appears employer-driven, top performers still get to choose where they work. The best talent isn't sitting on the sidelines. They're being selective. And the organizations that recognize that are the ones consistently winning the hiring race. #OrlandoBusiness #HiringManagers #Recruiting #TalentAcquisition #FloridaBusiness #TechHiring #Leadership #HumanResources #OrlandoJobs #HiringStrategy … more",
