      "id": "LI00265",
      "sourceId": "LI00265",
      "url": null,
      "text": "The U.S. Job Market Is Picking Up, But Finding the Right Talent Isn't Easy There's been some interesting movement in the U.S. job market lately. New data shows that job openings increased in September, with stronger demand across manufacturing, transportation, and professional services. That's encouraging news for businesses and job seekers. But I think there's another side to this. Having more open positions doesn't necessarily mean companies are finding the right people. Many employers are looking for specific skills and practical experience, while candidates are trying to understand what companies actually value. From a business perspective, hiring isn't just about filling vacancies. It's about finding people who can contribute, adapt, and grow with the organization. And for job seekers, staying relevant and continuing to develop useful skills matters more than ever. The job market may be changing, but the importance of good people hasn't changed. For those involved in hiring, what is harder right now: finding qualified candidates or keeping good employees? #USJobMarket #Hiring #CareerDevelopment #HumanResources #BusinessLeadership #Workforce … more",
