      "id": "LI00270",
      "sourceId": "LI00270",
      "url": null,
      "text": "The U.S. Job Market Is Moving, But Hiring Is Still a Challenge There's something interesting happening in the U.S. job market. Recent ADP data shows that private employers added 86,000 jobs in October, which is better than many economists expected. That's encouraging, but I don't think the bigger story is just the number of jobs being added. Companies are still being careful about who they hire. Many businesses want experienced people who can step in, understand the work, and contribute without a long learning curve. At the same time, job seekers are facing a different kind of challenge. Having experience doesn't always mean finding the right opportunity is easy. I think employers need to look beyond a resume and pay more attention to practical skills, adaptability, and the ability to work with others. A strong business isn't built by hiring the most people. It's built by bringing in the right people. For those involved in hiring, what's harder today: finding qualified candidates or finding people who are the right fit for the company? #USJobMarket #Hiring #CareerDevelopment #BusinessLeadership #HumanResources #Employment … more",
