      "url": null,
      "text": "Yesterday I said I’d show a bit behind the curtain. Here’s an early look. This is the governance side of Prisym, just a skeleton for my own demoing to people. Paste in a job posting, or point it at a careers site. It reads what’s in there and shows you what it found before anything goes anywhere. Then nothing becomes “the answer” until a named person approves it. The talent architect reviews the role content, the hiring manager guides on team needs and increases ownership of the hiring process, finance is looped in for pay and benefits, and an admin controls who can do what. It’s early, and we’re opening it to a small group of in-house TA teams who want to shape it. Have our initial partners but I am eager to get the product out into the wild and working with as many users as possible so we can iterate and deliver on what the TA function needs. Built with Cathal, Gary and Jorge and with thanks to lots of input from our network to date. I believe there are so many downstream benefits to come from this across compliance, AI effectiveness, hiring experience across TA, hiring managers and candidates and a greater alignment across the People function. shoot me a message or look out for me reaching out and be sound and give us some time … more",
