      "url": null,
      "text": "Looking for a remote job is strange these days. I have the experience. I speak the language. I can do everything the job asks for. And still, it is so hard to find a role that is really remote. Many job posts say “remote”, but then I read the details: • “Only candidates living in Germany” • “Must be in the office once a week” • “Remote, but only in this one country” For me, remote means one thing: I can work from anywhere, do my tasks, join every team meeting and work on European time. That’s it. A little about me: German and Hungarian speaking e-commerce and customer support specialist, with experience in order management, returns, logistics coordination and back-office work. I also ran my own online shop for three years. If your team is hiring for a truly remote role in e-commerce support, order management or admin, I would be happy to talk. And if you are a recruiter: please write “remote” only when it is really remote. 🙂 #remotework #ecommerce #customersupport #germanspeaking #hiring … more",
