      "id": "LI00498",
      "sourceId": "LI00498",
      "url": null,
      "text": "Remote work is real. So are the scams built around it. I’ve seen too many people lose money chasing remote jobs. Before you accept any remote offer, check for these 3 red flags 🚩 1. They ask you to pay for the job Training fees, equipment fees, registration fees. Real employers pay you. They do not charge you. 2. The whole interview happens on WhatsApp or Telegram No video call. No company email. You are hired within minutes. A real company has a real process. 3. High pay for no skills $3,000 a month to like posts is not a job. If you cannot describe the job or verify the company, it may not exist. A quick way to verify any offer: → Check the company’s LinkedIn page → Search the company name plus “scam” → Confirm the recruiter’s email domain Swipe through the slides and save this for your next application. Have you seen a fake job offer before? Tell me in the comments Repost to protect someone who is job hunting right now. Follow me for more remote work tips. … more",
