      "url": null,
      "text": "One thing I wish more people understood about remote work is that wanting a remote job and being prepared for one are two different things. I get messages from people asking me to give them a remote job. I understand the urgency, and I know many people genuinely need the opportunity. But remote jobs aren’t handed out simply because you ask for them. You need relevant skills, practical knowledge, confidence using digital tools, a good understanding of the role you’re applying for, and the ability to communicate your value to an employer. That’s why learning matters. You don’t need to know everything before you begin, but you do need to be willing to learn, practice, improve, and put yourself out there. If getting a remote job is one of your goals, make preparing for the opportunity part of the goal too. #remotework #remotejobs #careerdevelopment #digitalSkills #virtualassistant … more",
