      "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7523767762788294656/",
      "text": "🚨 If I had to find a job in 2026, I'd stop doing these 6 things manually. I'd use AI to find better opportunities, improve my CV, research companies, and prepare for interviews. 🌐 REMOTE JOB WEBSITES Looking for work-from-home opportunities? Start here. 👇 → Remote Rocketship Explore 100,000+ work-from-home job listings. [link hidden] → Remotive Find curated remote job opportunities, especially in tech. [link hidden] Here are 6 AI tools I'd use to job hunt smarter. 👇 1️⃣ FIND JOBS WITHOUT ENDLESS SCROLLING ❌ Old way: Search job boards for hours. ✅ Smarter way: Use ChatGPT to refine your search, then verify openings on Indeed. Try this prompt: \"Help me find remote jobs that match my skills, accept applicants from my country, and offer UK-hour overlap. Give me relevant search terms and criteria to check.\" 2️⃣ STOP SENDING THE SAME CV EVERYWHERE ❌ Old way: One generic resume for every job. ✅ Smarter way: Use Kickresume to tailor your CV to each job description. ✓ Highlight relevant experience ✓ Include measurable achievements ✓ Emphasise relevant skills ✓ Remove irrelevant details Never let AI invent experience or qualifications. 3️⃣ RESEARCH THE COMPANY BEFORE APPLYING ❌ Old way: Read random reviews and guess what matters. ✅ Smarter way: Use Claude to research the company. Ask: → What does the company sell? → Who are its customers? → What has changed recently? → What challenges might this role solve? Always verify the sources. 4️⃣ PRACTISE BEFORE THE INTERVIEW ❌ Old way: Watch interview videos and hope you're ready. ✅ Smarter way: Use Yoodli to practise speaking and receive feedback. Improve your clarity, confidence, pacing, and ability to explain your experience. Practise delivering your answers out loud. 5️⃣ SHOW YOUR SKILLS, NOT JUST YOUR RESUME ❌ Old way: List your skills and hope recruiters notice. ✅ Smarter way: Use Gamma to build a professional 5-slide case study. Slide 1: The problem Slide 2: Your role Slide 3: Your approach Slide 4: Results Slide 5: Lessons learned Use real projects and genuine results. 6️⃣ TRACK EVERY APPLICATION ❌ Old way: Forget where you applied and when to follow up. ✅ Smarter way: Use Notion to organise your job search. Track job links, companies, CV versions, application dates, interview stages, and follow-ups. 📚 GOOGLE COURSES TO UPGRADE YOUR SKILLS IN 2026 → Google Data Analytics [link hidden] → Google Project Management [link hidden] → Foundations of Project Management [link hidden] → Google Introduction to Generative AI [link hidden] → Google Cybersecurity [link hidden] 💡 THE BIGGEST MISTAKE JOB SEEKERS MAKE? ♻️ REPOST it to help someone job hunting in 2026. 👇 What's your biggest job-search challenge right now? #AI #JobSearch #CareerGrowth #ResumeTips #JobSeekers … more",
