      "url": null,
      "text": "Remote Work Is a Skillset Too… Being good at your technical job does not automatically mean you are good at remote work. Remote teams often depend heavily on: • Written communication • Time management • Self-management • Documentation • Digital collaboration • Follow-through • Clear updates • Meeting etiquette • Asking for help early • Managing priorities Imagine your manager asks: “What did you complete today?” A strong remote worker can give a concise update: DONE: • Reconciled 24 customer records • Replied to outstanding enquiries • Updated CRM NEXT: • Follow up with 6 customers • Prepare Friday report BLOCKED: • Waiting for access to the billing dashboard That is remote professionalism. You are making your work visible without someone standing beside you. Remote readiness is not just “I can work from home.” It is the ability to communicate, organise and deliver without constant supervision. Start sending yourself daily DONE / NEXT / BLOCKED updates for one week. You are practising a remote-work habit before you even get the job. #RemoteJobs #RemoteWork #JobSearch #CareerTips #JobSeekers #WorkFromHome #RemoteCareer #6000RemoteJobSeekers … more",
