      "id": "LI00608",
      "sourceId": "LI00608",
      "url": null,
      "text": "Remote experience is useful, but it isn’t the only way to demonstrate remote-work readiness. Candidates can build credible proof by showing how they communicate, organize tasks, use workplace tools, solve problems, and work independently. A simple portfolio might include: • A professional email • A mock project tracker • A customer-support response • A short screen-recorded process walkthrough Examples from retail, school, volunteering, caregiving, freelancing, and personal projects can also support your case. Describe the situation, your actions, and the result. Add metrics only when they’re accurate. Finally, tailor that proof to the posting. Look for repeated requirements such as written communication, customer service, spreadsheets, scheduling, data entry, troubleshooting, CRM systems, or ticketing tools. Don’t overclaim remote experience. Show that you already have the habits and transferable skills needed to succeed. [link hidden] … more",
