      "text": "\"Remote\" still mostly means remote in the US. 🌍 New on the Remote1st blog: the first Remote1st Remote Work Index. We deduplicated every remote job in our index, 14,640 unique jobs from 1,186 employers, and asked who can apply, which ads show pay, and what that pay is. Key findings: • Two in three remote jobs (67.7%) are open to US residents only. Just 29.0% can hire someone in the UK or the EU. • \"Work from anywhere\" is rare: only 119 jobs (0.8%) give a worldwide or \"anywhere\" location. • 58.9% of US remote ads state a salary, against 26.7% in the UK and 22.2% in the EU. • Among salaried roles open to UK residents, 204 quote pay in USD and 89 in GBP. • Canada's remote market is mostly an extension of the US one: 94.8% of Canada-open roles are also open to US residents. Read the full index 👉 [link hidden] Every Remote1st listing shows where the employer can hire from. Free weekly job alerts are available for the USA, UK, Canada and Europe. Remote1st. Remote jobs ranked right. #RemoteWork #RemoteJobs #PayTransparency #JobSearch … more",
