      "id": "LI00717",
      "sourceId": "LI00717",
      "url": null,
      "text": "I've talked before about bosses who expect everyone back in the office while they're working from home themselves. To be fair to them, there's another side to it. When you're a business owner, I think you kind of earn the right to say I've got to get that work-life balance right. There's enough pressure in being a business owner. I'm not going to deny that if you're running a business that's linked to your home and you could lose your home if the business fails. That's a lot of pressure. But people working for you are feeling the pressure of the world at the moment as well. They need some time not travelling into the office, the odd lie-in, a few things that don't break the norm, and I think that's a good thing. So give yourself the balance, and give it to your team as well. It's a lot easier to hire for a business that does. … more",
