      "url": null,
      "text": "Candidates, please stop making this mistake. We ask a candidate: “What is your current salary?” They tell us their number, then immediately say: “I know it’s high, and I don’t mind taking less.” Wait… why? How did you decide that your salary is high before even knowing the salary range for the new role? In many cases, the range offered by the employer is actually higher than what the candidate is currently earning. Don’t negotiate against yourself. First, understand the role, responsibilities, market value, and the employer’s salary range. Then have a conversation about compensation. You might be willing to take less for the right opportunity, and that’s completely fine. But don’t offer to lower your salary before anyone even asks you to. Know your value. Ask questions. And never assume you’re being paid too much without knowing what the opportunity actually offers. … more",
