      "id": "LI00802",
      "sourceId": "LI00802",
      "url": null,
      "text": "You find a job that matches your experience. Then the application asks for your salary expectations. But there's no salary range in the job description. 😅 Now you're left wondering what figure to put. Ask for too much, and you risk being ruled out. Ask for too little, and you could end up undervaluing your experience. I understand that salaries can vary depending on the responsibilities, experience required, and location. But even an estimated range would help candidates make informed decisions before applying. 📌 Personally, I'd rather know early on whether my expectations match the company's budget than find out after several interviews. Both candidates and hiring teams invest time in the recruitment process. A little transparency can save everyone that time. Recruiters and hiring managers, I'm genuinely curious. What makes it difficult to include a salary range in job postings? … more",
