      "id": "LI00803",
      "sourceId": "LI00803",
      "url": null,
      "text": "Could \"competitive salary\" be putting people off applying for your vacancy? In our recent poll, 43% of respondents said they would not apply for a job without a salary range. We asked whether people would apply for a role that only described the pay as \"competitive\". Here's what they told us: - 25% would apply if the role appealed. - 43% would not apply without a salary range. - 16% would ask about pay first. - 16% said it depends on the employer. Salary won't be someone's only consideration. However, knowing whether a role meets their financial needs helps them decide whether to explore it further. For hiring firms, leaving out the salary could mean missing an application from someone with the experience you need. It also creates an extra step for candidates who want to clarify pay before applying. Including a realistic salary range, alongside clear information about responsibilities, benefits and working arrangements, helps people make an informed decision. If the range depends on experience, explain what you're looking for at each level. Thank you to everyone who voted and shared their views. #SalaryTransparency #Recruitment #Hiring … more",
