      "id": "LI00812",
      "sourceId": "LI00812",
      "url": null,
      "text": "A recruiter reached out to me last week about an open position at a transportation company. Run the whole operation: dispatch, routing, maintenance, and everything in between. The more I read, the more interested I got. It was everything I know and everything I can do. Then I hit the bottom: \"competitive compensation.\" We all know what that means, and I usually keep scrolling. But this time a real person reached out to me, so I set up a phone screen. The call went great. We covered what I do, what they need, and everything lined up. Then we got to the compensation, and it was worse than I expected: → 5 days in the office → On call whenever I'm not there → Responsible for the entire operation → Average benefits → Well under market, no bonus Forget how far below market that is. This is exactly why salary ranges need to be posted. Job searching is already hard and time-consuming. Stop wasting people's time. #SalaryTransparency #Hiring #Recruiting #Transportation #Logistics … more",
