      "id": "LI00815",
      "sourceId": "LI00815",
      "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7522926795848056832/",
      "text": "Asked for a bit less than the top of their own salary range. Offer pulled. Straight away. A candidate told me about this recently. The job ad said \"up to\" a number. He came back just under it. The reply: \"You clearly don't value our offer.\" He sent a polite email back. Never heard anything again. Months later, the job was still open. 🙃 I get it. Budgets are tight, and nobody wants to start with a tough negotiation. But a counter inside your own advertised range isn't greed. It's someone who read your job ad. And every candidate who hears this story negotiates a little less next time. Or doesn't apply. Ever had an offer pulled because you negotiated? … more",
