      "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7523863590634921985/",
      "text": "Jimminy Crickets!!!! Alright, let me lay this out in a simple ELI5 way for recruiters on LinkedIn that still don't get it. Here is how your interaction should start with an individual you are reaching out to for a role. Hello {Persons Name}, {your short intro if you so choose} I have the following position available and I feel like you would be a good fit due to your experience {listed position/experience on profile}. This role is {on-site/hybrid/fully remote} based out of {location} The salary range for this position is {Insert salary range in whatever currency} I have attached the job description below. If this seems like a good fit for you, could you send a recent copy of your resume over and we can arrange a time to talk more. That is it. Don't make the candidate pull details out of you like pulling teeth. Don't hide details or omit them. Give them the BLUF (Bottom Line Up Front) Position Location Pay Job Description Stop wasting your time and our time sending bland messages that we are a great fit for a position and force us to dig the details out of you. … more",
