      "text": "$130,000. That's where an Assistant Superintendent's range starts right now $130,000. That's also where a Superintendent's range starts Two different titles. The exact same floor. The ranges I'm placing at right now: Assistant Superintendent: $130,000+ Superintendent: $130,000–$200,000 An Assistant Super and a Superintendent can walk onto the same jobsite making the exact same base. The title on the business card tells you nothing about the number until you know the ceiling, not the floor. What separates them isn't the starting pay. It's whether someone's running the job solo or still working under a Superintendent's call — and that only shows up at the top of the range, not the bottom. If you're budgeting an Assistant Super role off \"entry-level pay,\" you might already be offering Superintendent money without realizing it. … more",
