      "url": null,
      "text": "120.000 € – 150.000 € a year. This can be the salary range for Boutique Managers of high-end luxury brands on the most prestigious luxury shopping streets in Europe. For many people outside the industry, this is surprising for a retail position. But Boutique Managers are responsible for 8 or in some cities even 9 digits of yearly sales revenue. That means a single boutique can generate as much annual revenue as an entire mid-sized company. Beyond that, they manage relationships with high-net-worth clients who spend over 200.000 € a year on leather goods, ready-to-wear, beauty and fine jewelry. These relationships are extremely valuable and demand a high level of personal commitment. At this level, clients don’t just bond with a brand but with the people representing it. So it is crucial to have the right people in that position. A Boutique Manager isn't just \"store staff\", they are running a multi-million euro business. They are essentially the CEO of that boutique. … more",
