      "id": "LI00825",
      "sourceId": "LI00825",
      "url": null,
      "text": "One thing I've noticed while applying for SEO jobs is how many companies ask for salary expectations without sharing their budget. And honestly, I never know what number they expect me to give. 😅 Ask for too much, and you might lose the opportunity before getting an interview. Ask for too little, and you risk undervaluing your experience. I personally prefer job listings that include a salary range, even if it's just an estimate. It saves both sides time and helps candidates decide whether the opportunity is worth pursuing. I've also learned that salary expectations are easier to discuss when you understand the responsibilities of the role. I'm curious, especially from agency owners and hiring managers. What's stopping more companies from including salary ranges in their job postings..? … more",
