      "id": "LI00827",
      "sourceId": "LI00827",
      "url": null,
      "text": "In almost every initial discovery call with hiring managers this quarter, pay transparency comes up: \"Should we post the exact salary range, or will it limit our negotiating room?\" My perspective from running talent solutions at Randstad: Hiding pay ranges doesn't protect your budget—it costs you your strongest candidates before the first conversation even happens. Here is what the data and daily candidate sentiment show: 1. Immediate drop-off: Top-tier performers rarely apply to \"competitive salary\" blind postings when they have multiple direct inbound offers with clear numbers. 2. Wasted interview cycles: Finding out in round 4 that your budget and their expectation are $30k apart is a massive drain on your hiring team's time. 3. Trust starts with clarity: Candidates view clear pay bands as an indicator of internal equity and healthy leadership culture. Posting realistic ranges isn't just about compliance—it's an operational filter that protects your hiring team's bandwidth. How has your team adapted its approach to compensation transparency over the past year? #RandstadKnoxville #RandstadUSA #TogetherWeGrow #PartnerForTalent #HereToHelp #Staffing #Trends … more",
