      "id": "LI00830",
      "sourceId": "LI00830",
      "url": null,
      "text": "What do employers post for pay? We read the pay ranges on their own careers sites, and this month the answer to the AI question depends on how you ask it. The Xcout Pay Pulse, October 2026: - 95,706 salaried US postings from 4,851 employers carried a pay range. The median midpoint: $138,400. - Within the same job family and seniority, postings that ask for AI skills advertise a median 17% more across all employers (79 comparisons, 75 pointing the same way). - Inside one employer, for the same family and seniority, the median gap is zero (840 comparisons at 306 employers). - So the premium mostly reflects which employers ask for AI. Account executives: +48% across employers, −5.6% inside the same one. - By state, California's postings lead at $172,325, then Washington at $165,000. - Posted pay beside H-1B application wages for six occupations, with what that comparison cannot show. Every figure shows the postings and employers behind it. Open to read without an account: [link hidden] … more",
