      "text": "We’re hiring on the Berkeley Global team at UC Berkeley Extension! We’re looking for a Career & Alumni Services Manager to build and run the career side of our visiting student programs. This role is part program manager, part educator. You’d design and develop career-focused programs and curriculum, recruit and supervise the instructors who teach them, and set the standards we use to measure whether they’re working. You’d also teach a non-credit career development workshop or course each semester, help evaluate new partnerships, and work with partners on the programs we already run. Our students come from all over the world, so cross-cultural skills matter a lot here. If you’ve managed academic or career programs in higher ed, especially with international students, and you like the mix of strategy, teaching, and day-to-day operations, please take a look. It’s a full-time career position, and the salary range is $95,000–$102,000. Apply here: [link hidden] Please share with anyone in your network who’d be a great fit, and feel free to message me if you have questions about working with us. … more",
