      "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7523003159976497152/",
      "text": "The Egyptian job market for marketing and advertising has become a complete circus, and everyone is pretending it’s normal. Pure clutter. High signal-to-noise ratio, zero efficiency. Every single day, the timeline is flooded with the exact same noise: \"Hiring a Senior Brand Strategist! Competitive package! Great culture!\" Great culture where? For what company? Why is the company name hidden like it’s a national security secret? If a brand is too embarrassed or paranoid to attach its own name to a hiring post, why should any top-tier talent trust them with their career? \"Salary Negotiable\" In 2026? Hiding the salary range isn't \"standard protocol\", it’s a power play. It wastes weeks of multi-stage interviews, assignment submissions, and back-and-forth emails, only to reveal an offer that doesn't even cover the candidate's operational baseline. Transparency isn't a perk; it's basic professional respect. If you want world-class strategists, creatives, and account leaders to take your agency or brand seriously, start with the absolute bare minimum. #Advertising #Marketing #Recruitment #SalaryTransparency #HiringStandards #CorporateCulture #CareerDevelopment #JobMarket … more",
