      "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7522211968619925507/",
      "text": "“What are your salary expectations?” You’ve found a job that looks perfect. You’ve got the experience, the skills and you’re ready to apply. Then you hit that question. What number do you put? Too high and you might get rejected before anyone reads your CV. Too low and you could be undervaluing yourself by thousands. So you Google average salaries, second guess yourself and hope you’ve picked the right number. Meanwhile, the company already has an approved salary budget. It’s an operational expense. Of course they’ve budgeted for it. They know the range. You’re left guessing. And somehow, your answer could determine whether you even get an interview. Salary transparency shouldn’t be this complicated. How many opportunities have candidates missed simply because they guessed the wrong number? #Recruitment #SalaryTransparency #JobSearch … more",
