      "url": null,
      "text": "Things that scare people in a senior job search, ranked. (Happy Halloween.) → Being told you're the top candidate, followed by three weeks of silence. → “You're a great candidate, but we're concerned you might be overqualified.” → Getting to the final round after six interviews, only to hear they've decided to hire internally. → “Can you explain this gap on your resume?” When it's already something you feel self-conscious about. → Finding a role that looks perfect, until you see the salary range is $50K below what you're making. And perhaps the scariest of all: Spending six months applying to jobs and barely getting any interviews, let alone offers. What would you add to the list? … more",
