      "id": "LI00837",
      "sourceId": "LI00837",
      "url": null,
      "text": "What’s spooky? Assistant principal salary averages trail entry-level remote salary averages in most geographic regions. If one of these leaders wants to leave their school-based role and jump into an entry-level, independent contributor remote role, they are looking at a salary range midpoint average between $86k and $112k across consulting, sales, or operations. Here are the current numbers: ASST. PRINCIPAL - California = $107k - Northeast = $104k - Pacific & Mountain West = $93k - Midwest = $83k - Southeast = $76k - Southwest = $76k ENTRY LEVEL REMOTE - Sales/Partnerships = $112k (98 jobs) - Operations = $107k (24 jobs) - Academic Consulting = $86k (40 jobs) - Academic Program Mgmt. = $86k (6 jobs) These are based on November 2026 salary range averages for all posted job listings on the jobs blast. California and the Northeastern US lead the way with salary averages (cost of living) between $104k and $107k as the midpoint. The Southeast and Southwest hover around $76k. That’s a challenge for school systems. We know about the transitioning teacher trend. What about the transitioning administrator? When teachers and leaders churn because of policies we set, it causes issues for other school staff, students, and families. Yes, more funding would be the magical solution. I also know that’s not one within our immediate control as school or system leaders. I wonder if there are ways to yield cost savings in other departments or budget line items to direct more money towards faculty and leader salary lines? I’ve seen this with new RFPs for operational services at the school level, finding additional grant dollars to support facilities enhancements or maintenance projects, or figuring out how to get more grant reimbursement for dollars you are already spending. A commitment to mission can only pay so many bills. … more",
