      "url": null,
      "text": "Hiring Myth: “Candidates who ask about salary first only care about money.” Asking about pay early is smart planning, not a red flag. It can feel a little forward when salary comes up in the first conversation. But candidates have bills, families and other offers to weigh. They’re trying to make sure the opportunity is realistic before everyone invests time. The best hiring outcomes come from transparency on both sides, which builds trust and keeps your process moving with candidates who are serious. Clear pay talk isn’t greedy. It’s respectful of everyone’s time. Do you share pay ranges in your job posts? 💭 #HiringMyths #BetterHires #IdealTraits #CandidateExperience #EmployerBrand … more",
