      "text": "\"What are your salary expectations?\" is the question most candidates want to skip. Name a number too early and it sticks; dodge it and you sound unsure. A better answer is a range. Research what the role pays, give a range whose bottom is a number you would happily take, and say you're open to talking about the whole package. A researched range shows you know what the work is worth, and it leaves room for the conversation. #interviewtips #careeradvice #jobsearch #hiring #recruiting … more",
