      "url": null,
      "text": "Prague job-ad starter pack: ✅MultiSport card ✅ Stravenky (meal vouchers) ✅ 5 weeks vacation ✅Fresh fruits in the office 🔒Salary: \"competitive\" Everything is clear about fruits. How much they pay is still a mystery. But in the form of a response, they immediately ask: \"Your salary expectations in CZK? *\" The field is required, of course. It turns out that I have to give my figure, but the company will hold its own for now. I like these bonuses. And I’m always ready to talk about money. I just wish I could at least roughly understand how much the position is calculated for. What if we spend time responding, texting, and making the first call to find out that our expectations don't overlap at all? Even an approximate range would help to understand this in advance. Question for recruiters and hiring managers in Prague: What usually prevents you from specifying a salary range in a vacancy? … more",
