      "id": "LI00871",
      "sourceId": "LI00871",
      "url": null,
      "text": "An incredible 1 in 3 of our members say the Women’s Sport Collective has helped them find a new role in sport. Of all the findings from our annual membership research, this is one that makes Kate Hannon and me especially proud. We love the incredible, supportive community that's grown around the Women's Sport Collective, but what matters most is the tangible difference it's making to women's careers in sport. Helping women discover new opportunities, make valuable connections and progress in an industry they love has always been at the heart of what we do and our Jobs Board is an important part of that. Right now, there are over 100 opportunities in sport listed, and every one includes a salary or salary range. It's something we've insisted on from the start as we believe salary transparency is a small but significant step towards making recruitment in sport fairer. It helps women make informed decisions about which roles to pursue, removes some of the uncertainty around pay and challenges the inequalities that can persist when salaries are hidden. So here are seven jobs in sport that caught my eye this week. 👇 Across the full Jobs Board, you'll find everything from entry-level opportunities to senior leadership and CEO positions, with salaries ranging from around £25k to over £100k. And it's completely free to access as a member of the Women's Sport Collective. In fact, everything we offer is free, from networking events and professional development to regional communities, webinars, funded event opportunities and our Fearless leadership programme. We're now a global community of more than 17,000 women working across sport and physical activity, supporting one another, sharing opportunities and helping each other progress. We'd love you to join our free community here: [link hidden] And if you're recruiting in sport, please do share your vacancies on our Jobs Board. It's completely free to advertise… as long as you include the salary or salary range! Share a job here: [link hidden] Please do share this post with any women who might benefit from discovering new opportunities in sport. 🧡 … more",
