      "id": "LI00878",
      "sourceId": "LI00878",
      "url": null,
      "text": "I think we need to have a conversation about salary expectations because, what exactly are we doing? 😭😂 You see a job advert. The salary range is clearly stated. You read it, apply, and get shortlisted. Then I call for a quick conversation before scheduling your interview, just to confirm that you're comfortable with the stated range. Suddenly, the salary is no longer okay. 😭 Now we're negotiating. We're explaining. We're going back and forth. But wait… wasn't the salary right there in the advert? 👀 Please, if the salary doesn't work for you, that's completely fine. You have every right to decline an opportunity. Maybe you're worth more. Maybe you have different expectations. No hard feelings. But applying for a role when the advertised salary is already outside your expectations, only to raise the issue when the recruitment process begins, wastes everyone's time. And honestly, recruitment already has enough delays. 😂 Of course, there's nothing wrong with negotiating when there's room to do so. But let's not confuse negotiation with applying for an opportunity you already know doesn't align with your expectations. So candidates, please read the advert before applying. If the salary range, role, or conditions don't align with what you're looking for, it's okay to move on. Reading the advert is the first interview. ❤️ … more",
