      "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7522278407934689282/",
      "text": "₹10–15 LPA vs ₹14–24 LPA: Same Backend Industry, But Why Such a BIG Salary Difference? 👀 Recently, while searching for a new job, I came across something that genuinely caught my attention! I have 3+ years of experience in Angular + Node.js, and while exploring the current job market, I noticed an interesting salary difference. Here is what I observed: Angular + Node.js Developer ₹10–15 LPA Golang Backend Developer ₹14–24 LPA These are salary ranges I came across in job openings, not guaranteed market averages. Now, this made me think... Is the programming language you choose really impacting your salary growth? Or are companies willing to pay more for specific backend skills and architecture experience? A few questions came to my mind: 1. Why are some companies offering higher packages for Golang developers? 2. Is Go becoming a preferred choice for high-performance backend systems? 3. Is Node.js losing its competitive advantage, or is it still equally valuable? 4. Should developers with 3+ years of Node.js experience consider switching to Go? My biggest question: If you already have 3+ years of experience in Node.js, would you continue with it or invest your time in learning Golang for better career growth? I would love to hear honest opinions from experienced developers, tech leads and recruiters. Let's discuss this with real industry insights! #Golang #NodeJS #BackendDeveloper #SalaryGrowth #TechCareers #SoftwareDevelopment #IndiaTech … more",
