      "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7523776093888196608/",
      "text": "😡 𝗦𝗼𝗺𝗲 𝗰𝗼𝗺𝗽𝗮𝗻𝗶𝗲𝘀... 🧑‍💻 Had a talk with a field service engineer of a previous employer of mine as he was searching for something new. He had an interview round with a large US-based machine manufacturer. Gone through all of it. 💰 Everything was fine regarding the salary. Or at least it seemed like it. Although I told him \"We're going to sort this out\" was not exactly a confirmation of his expectation. Can see the reason why it's understood like that though. 📜 And then the contract came for signing and it was 20% less than his MINIMUM salary range. 🤦‍♂️ That's basically the prime example how employers can waste time. Not only time of the applicant but even their own. Where's the saying \"time is money\" in such a case, I'm wondering? 😈 When I wouldn't have something better to do (like working for my salary, you know), I would be so tempted to just apply for fun at these companies to waste some of their own time... … more",
