      "id": "LI00911",
      "sourceId": "LI00911",
      "url": null,
      "text": "Imagine landing a Strategic PMO leadership role with a salary range reaching US$410,000 annually. Now imagine the responsibility that comes with it. PwC’s posting for Managed Services - Strategic PMO Director caught my attention, and I wanted to share it with my network. 📍 Boca Raton, Florida | Listed as onsite, full-time 💰 Published salary range: $155,000–$410,000, plus eligibility for an annual discretionary bonus. The upper figure is the maximum advertised, not a guaranteed offer. Compensation depends on experience, skills, qualifications, and location. What stands out to me is the combination of responsibilities. This leader will oversee delivery across multiple client programs, guide portfolio priorities and resource allocation, support benefits realization, build executive relationships, and develop emerging leaders. And there is another expectation PMO professionals should pay attention to: Business development. PwC explicitly includes leading business development efforts, identifying market gaps, and contributing thought leadership. That adds a commercial dimension to PMO leadership: understanding client needs, earning trust, and helping grow the business while delivering results. The stated minimums include a bachelor’s degree and at least eight years of experience. But meeting the minimums and demonstrating readiness are different achievements. My advice: make your evidence visible. • Which complex portfolios have you led? • How did your prioritization decisions improve outcomes? • What benefits were realized? • How have you earned executive clients’ trust? • What business opportunities have you helped develop? • Who became a stronger leader because of your coaching? After more than four decades in the workplace, I encourage professionals to read job descriptions as development maps. Even if this opportunity is not your next move, it can help you identify the capabilities to build for the move after that. For those with managed services, consulting, and strategic PMO leadership experience, this role deserves a closer look. What is the biggest stretch for PMO leaders moving into consulting leadership: commercial growth, executive relationships, or delivery across multiple clients? I’m sharing independently to support my network. Review the full posting and apply through PwC if your experience aligns. Know someone who fits? Pass this opportunity along. Follow Dr. Tony Prensa for PMO and project leadership opportunities, practical career insights, and conversations about creating business value. #PMOLeadership #ExecutiveCareers #StrategicPMO #jobs #pmojobs … more",
