      "sourceId": "LI00919",
      "url": null,
      "text": "Walmart | Group Director, Product Marketing First, that salary range. $160K to $320K. For the same job. That quite a spread. 🧐 Graymatter Executive Opportunity Review Graymatter isn't affiliated with Walmart or this role. We review opportunities because your time is too valuable to waste pursuing the wrong ones. Graymatter Score: Clarity A- | Executive Appeal A- | Role Design B What This Job Really Is This is one of the broadest product marketing jobs we've reviewed. Walmart wants someone to connect its app, fulfillment, services, in-store experiences, emerging products and local marketing into one coherent customer proposition. And this matters more than ever. Walmart generated $713B in revenue last year, its advertising business grew 46%, and roughly 23% of Walmart U.S. sales are now eCommerce. The company is becoming much more than a retailer. This leader helps customers understand that. You'll Probably Love This If... You've led large-scale consumer product marketing and know how to move from product insight to commercialization, adoption and lifecycle growth. You understand physical and digital customer journeys and are comfortable influencing Product, eCommerce, Stores, Merchandising, Technology and Marketing at the same time. You'll also lead a large multidisciplinary organization, so this is real enterprise leadership. This Probably Isn't Your Role If... You want a clean product portfolio or simple decision-making. This remit includes almost everything between \"Walmart built something\" and \"customers actually use it.\" That's powerful. It's also a lot of stakeholders. Before You Apply 1. What products and services are actually highest priority? 2. How large is the team and budget? 3. What decisions does this leader truly own versus influence? 4. And how will success be weighted across app adoption, fulfillment usage, store behavior, retention and local-market performance? 5. Then there's compensation. 6. The stated base is $160K–$320K plus bonus and potentially stock. That's not a salary band. That's almost two different jobs. I'd want to understand the target hiring range very early. The Graymatter Take This is a consequential role. Walmart already has extraordinary scale. The opportunity is to make its increasingly complex ecosystem feel simple and useful to customers. That requires more than campaigns. It requires shaping products upstream, commercializing them effectively and driving adoption afterward. Excellent mandate. I'd just want to know whether the authority, resources and compensation all land in the same zip code. Good Luck! Follow me for more Graymatter Executive Opportunity Reviews. We look beyond the job description to help you decide which opportunities are worth pursuing. … more",
