      "text": "Employers in the EU will have to tell you the salary before your job interview 🇪🇺 And they will no longer be allowed to ask how much you earned in your previous job. These are 2 important requirements under the EU Pay Transparency Directive. The new rules require employers to: ✅ Inform candidates about the starting salary or salary range in the job advertisement or before the interview. ✅ Stop asking candidates about their salary history. ✅ Use gender neutral job advertisements and recruitment processes. The deadline for EU countries to introduce these rules was June 7, 2026. However, several countries are still working on implementing them. Germany has not yet completed the implementation, while countries such as Italy have already introduced new legislation. For jobseekers, this means you should pay attention to the salary transparency rules in the country where you are applying. You should know what a position pays before spending hours preparing for interviews. … more",
