      "id": "LI00947",
      "sourceId": "LI00947",
      "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7524029071131996160/",
      "text": "Let’s have an uncomfortable conversation about pay. 👀 Are salary bands really designed to create fairness, consistency and equal pay, or are they simply a mechanism for businesses to manage and contain their wage bill? It’s an interesting question, particularly as pay transparency becomes an increasingly important part of the reward agenda. If two people are delivering the same value, doing essentially the same job, but sitting at very different points on the salary scale, how do organisations justify that? And if a business can’t clearly explain how it determines someone’s position within a salary band, can it genuinely claim to have a fair and transparent reward strategy? I’d be interested in hearing some honest perspectives from both sides of the table. Let’s think about this… Are salary bands about fairness, or financial control?! 🤔 … more",
