      "url": null,
      "text": "Pay transparency is coming to Finland on 1 January 2027. 💼 The government has submitted a proposal to implement the EU Pay Transparency Directive. For employers, this means: 🔹 Salary or salary range must be shared with applicants, and asking about candidates’ previous pay is no longer allowed 🔹 Employees get stronger rights to information about pay criteria and average pay for equal work 🔹 Pay confidentiality clauses will be prohibited 🔹 If transparency obligations aren’t met, the burden of proof shifts to the employer 🔹 Gender pay gap reporting for larger employers (EU Directive: 100+ employees), expected to be introduced gradually in Finland And a reminder: employers with 30+ employees must already have an equality plan that includes a pay survey. The time to review recruitment processes, salary structures and pay policies is now, especially if you’re hiring in Finland without a local HR organisation. Read the full guide 👉 [link hidden] #PayTransparency #Finland #HR #Recruitment #EmployerGuide … more",
