      "id": "LI00954",
      "sourceId": "LI00954",
      "url": null,
      "text": "Ever wondered if a recruiter can legally ask about your current salary? In Europe, the rules of the game have officially changed. The EU Pay Transparency Directive has shifted the power dynamic in recruitment. The era of the \"Salary History Ban\" is here, meaning employers are increasingly prohibited from asking candidates about their past or current compensation. Here is where the law stands across Europe at the end of 2026. Countries where the ban is FULLY IN FORCE • Poland • Italy • Slovakia • Lithuania • Malta • Greece Countries finalising preparation (Bills launching late 2026 / early 2027) These nations have drafted official legislation, and the ban will fully take effect in the coming weeks or by early 2027: • Germany • France • Spain • Netherlands • Belgium • Denmark • Ireland • Czech Republic • Portugal • Finland • Romania, Bulgaria, Cyprus, Latvia, Estonia The Big Exception: United Kingdom Keep in mind that post-Brexit UK does not follow EU directives. British recruiters can still legally ask about your current salary in UK, leaving it up to your personal negotiation strategy. Have you been asked about your current salary during an interview recently? How did you handle it? Let’s discuss in the comments below! 👇 … more",
