      "id": "LI00955",
      "sourceId": "LI00955",
      "url": null,
      "text": "What do the US election results mean for employees and their pay? Based on legislation we've already seen in blue states, I believe we could see renewed efforts to establish national standards in several areas: 1. Increase in the federal minimum wage Currently $7.25 per hour, unchanged since 2009. 2. Increase in the FLSA salary threshold for overtime exemption Currently $35,568 annually 3. National pay transparency and pay equity legislation - Disclosure of salary ranges and benefits in job postings. - Prohibitions on employers asking candidates about salary history. - Stronger pay equity requirements including regular reporting and analysis. What do you think? Which of these changes is most likely? Are there other compensation-related legislative priorities we should be watching? How would these changes reshape the employee-employer relationship? #Compensation #TotalRewards #PayTransparency #PayEquity #FLSA #HumanResources #PerformComp … more",
