      "id": "LI00961",
      "sourceId": "LI00961",
      "url": null,
      "text": "One of the reasons employees leave jobs that nobody talks about enough. Recently, a candidate went through several interview stages. She was offered a job with a salary of ₦180,000. She accepted, resumed, and completed her first month. Then came the surprise. Her employer informed her that the ₦180,000 was actually target-based. Meet your target? You earn ₦180,000. Miss your target? You earn less. Now she’s considering leaving. And honestly, I understand why. You cannot recruit someone based on one salary structure and introduce another after they’ve resumed. If a salary is target-based, commission-based, or conditional on performance, communicate that from the beginning. Transparency doesn’t just help you hire. It helps you retain. Have you ever experienced something like this? … more",
