      "text": "Talking about your salary at work… should it really be taboo in 2026? For years, discussing pay with colleagues has been seen as something you just don't do. But times are changing. 👀 With pay transparency becoming a bigger talking point across the recruitment industry and last weeks discussion on Morning TV, it's raising some interesting questions. 💬 Why should two people doing the same job be uncomfortable discussing what they earn? 💬 Should employers be more open about salary bands? 💬 Could greater transparency help close pay gaps and build trust? 💬 Or could it create tension between colleagues? 🔥 I'd love to hear your thoughts… Should employees openly discuss their salaries with colleagues, or is pay better kept private? Let's get a discussion going. 👇 #PayTransparency #Recruitment #HR #SalaryTransparency #WorkplaceCulture #TalentAcquisition … more",
