      "id": "LI00975",
      "sourceId": "LI00975",
      "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7522998543675183104/",
      "text": "💷 What if you could find out what your colleagues REALLY earn? 👀 Same job. Same responsibilities. Different salary? And you might not even know it! 😳 Well, that could be about to change... Equality and Human Rights Commission is calling for NEW legal rights that would give employees greater transparency over what their colleagues are paid! 🙌 Here's what's being proposed: 💗 Pay transparency: Employers could be required to share information about colleagues' salaries, bonuses and overtime when formally requested. 💷 No more salary history questions: Employers could be stopped from asking what you currently earn when offering you a job. ⚖️ Fairer pay: The aim is to tackle pay discrimination and prevent historic pay inequalities from following women throughout their careers. And here's why it matters... If you've been underpaid in one role, why should that follow you into the next? Your next salary should reflect your skills, experience and VALUE. Not what your previous employer decided to pay you! 👏 These are proposals, NOT law just yet, but they could be a significant step towards greater pay fairness in the workplace. 💬 We want to know what YOU think! Would you feel comfortable knowing what your colleagues earn AND having them know your salary? Or do you think pay should remain private? 👇 📰 Read the full BBC article: [link hidden] #EqualPay #PayTransparency #WomenAtWork #GenderPayGap #InvestingInWomen #CareerConfidence … more",
