      "id": "LI00977",
      "sourceId": "LI00977",
      "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7523807142756343808/",
      "text": "A Question About PF Contributions and Salary Transparency – Something HR Needs to Address! Recently, I came across a salary structure that raised an important concern regarding the treatment of Employee and Employer PF contributions. While Employee PF contributions are deducted from an employee's salary, the Employer PF contribution is the statutory responsibility of the employer. However, in certain salary structures, employees may notice that the employer's PF contribution is also impacting their monthly take-home salary. This raises some important questions: 1. Why is the employer's PF contribution also reducing an employee's take-home salary? 2. If the employer's contribution is a statutory obligation, why is its financial impact being passed on to employees? 3. Are employees clearly informed about this adjustment during salary discussions? 4. Why isn't the distinction between Employee PF and Employer PF contributions explained transparently in the salary breakup? Including the employer's PF contribution in the overall CTC is understandable. However, deducting or adjusting it against an employee's agreed salary is a different matter and deserves proper clarification. Shouldn't employees have complete transparency about every component of their salary and every deduction affecting their monthly take-home pay? I would genuinely appreciate insights from HR leaders, payroll professionals and industry experts on this subject. Transparency in compensation should be a standard practice, not something employees have to investigate themselves. #hr #payroll #epfo #employee #retail #Hrpayroll … more",
