      "id": "LI00988",
      "sourceId": "LI00988",
      "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7523277172481089536/",
      "text": "The EU Pay Transparency Directive: An opportunity to improve more than compliance Don’t miss out on reaping the business benefits of your Pay Transparency work. The EU’s Pay Transparency Directive is expected to come into force on 1 March 2027 and sets new requirements for companies’ pay transparency, documentation, and reporting to reduce gender pay gaps. It is therefore crucial to be equipped to comply with the requirements. But why not take the opportunity to realize some of the additional business benefits outlined in my overview at the same time? As a former HR manager and business partner, HR data manager, and master data governance architect, I help more companies build job architectures. This structured model describes how a company’s positions, roles, responsibilities, remuneration, and competencies are related within job families and levels, among others. Beyond being a vital basis for Pay Transparency, it creates a clear career path for managers and employees, defines decision-making competencies and financial authority, establishes a transparent pay and compensation structure, and improves workforce planning for HR, management, and employees. This helps streamline the organization, reduce ambiguities that create noise in daily work, and provide a career path for employees who don't want to be managers. I'd like to hear how your work on pay transparency creates business value. #HR #PayTransparency #MasterDataGoverance #JobArchitectures #RealizedOpportunity … more",
