      "id": "LI00999",
      "sourceId": "LI00999",
      "url": null,
      "text": "Salary history questions can carry existing pay inequalities into a new role, the Equality and Human Rights Commission warns. The EHRC is calling for a ban on employers asking candidates about previous earnings or salary expectations. This is a recommendation, not confirmed government policy. Mary-Ann Stephenson, who chairs the EHRC, says publishing salaries in job adverts is a positive step. The regulator also wants employers to be required to respond to statutory pay questionnaires, helping workers access information about potential discrimination. Marie van der Zyl OBE, Employment Partner at Keystone Law, highlights an important balance: greater transparency could expose disparities earlier, but disclosure requirements would need clear boundaries to protect colleagues’ privacy. #PayTransparency #EqualPay #Recruitment Follow us for more HR news and insights! [link hidden] … more",
