      "id": "LI01001",
      "sourceId": "LI01001",
      "url": null,
      "text": "𝗣𝗮𝘆 𝗧𝗿𝗮𝗻𝘀𝗽𝗮𝗿𝗲𝗻𝗰𝘆: 𝗙𝗿𝗼𝗺 𝗖𝗼𝗺𝗽𝗹𝗶𝗮𝗻𝗰𝗲 𝘁𝗼 𝗦𝘁𝗿𝗮𝘁𝗲𝗴𝗶𝗰 𝗖𝗼𝗺𝗽𝗲𝗻𝘀𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻 𝗠𝗮𝗻𝗮𝗴𝗲𝗺𝗲𝗻𝘁 𝗜𝘀 𝘆𝗼𝘂𝗿 𝗼𝗿𝗴𝗮𝗻𝗶𝘇𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻 𝗿𝗲𝗮𝗱𝘆 𝘁𝗼 𝗺𝗼𝘃𝗲 𝗯𝗲𝘆𝗼𝗻𝗱 𝗰𝗼𝗺𝗽𝗹𝗶𝗮𝗻𝗰𝗲? With Greece's new pay transparency framework introducing significant changes, organizations face challenges that extend far beyond regulatory reporting. From establishing objective compensation criteria and clear job structures to ensuring reliable HR data and stronger governance, achieving readiness requires a strategic and coordinated approach. In his latest article, VAIOS PLAKOTIS, FCCA, 𝗗𝗶𝗿𝗲𝗰𝘁𝗼𝗿 𝗼𝗳 𝗢𝘂𝘁𝘀𝗼𝘂𝗿𝗰𝗶𝗻𝗴 at 𝗙𝗼𝗿𝘃𝗶𝘀 𝗠𝗮𝘇𝗮𝗿𝘀 𝗶𝗻 𝗚𝗿𝗲𝗲𝗰𝗲, explores the key regulatory changes, the challenges businesses face, and a practical three-step roadmap — 𝗔𝘀𝘀𝗲𝘀𝘀𝗺𝗲𝗻𝘁, 𝗗𝗲𝘀𝗶𝗴𝗻 𝗮𝗻𝗱 𝗜𝗺𝗽𝗹𝗲𝗺𝗲𝗻𝘁𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻 — to help organizations prepare for the new requirements. Pay transparency is not just about meeting legal obligations. It is about building a more transparent, consistent and well-documented approach to compensation management. Discover the key considerations and practical steps organizations should prioritize. 🔗 𝗥𝗲𝗮𝗱 𝘁𝗵𝗲 𝗳𝘂𝗹𝗹 𝗮𝗿𝘁𝗶𝗰𝗹𝗲: [link hidden] #ForvisMazarsinGreece #PayTransparency #CompensationManagement #HRTransformation #ThoughtLeadership Forvis Mazars Group … more",
