      "id": "LI01003",
      "sourceId": "LI01003",
      "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7523381967275319296/",
      "text": "Payslip Awareness: A Shared Responsibility Having managed payroll for over 15,000 employees, I have observed that only around 20% of employees review their payslips regularly every month. However, during April, March, and salary revision periods, payslip views typically increase to more than 80%. A payslip is more than a salary statement. It provides important information on earnings, tax deductions, PF contributions, and salary changes. Reviewing it monthly helps employees stay informed and address concerns proactively. Payroll is one of the most trusted functions within any organization. Every month, employees place their confidence in the payroll team to ensure salaries are processed accurately and on time. With that trust comes a significant responsibility. While payroll teams are responsible for delivering accurate pay, employees also have a responsibility to review their payslips regularly. Transparency, trust, and payroll accuracy are most effective when both payroll and employees work together. … more",
