      "id": "LI01024",
      "sourceId": "LI01024",
      "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7523761583949393920/",
      "text": "★ Ghost Job Detector ★ The pay range tells a story In BC, the Pay Transparency Act has required employers to include the expected pay or pay range in publicly advertised job postings since November 1, 2023. \"Competitive salary\" or \"up to $30/hour\" doesn't cut it. So when a BC posting has: → No pay at all, or → A range wide enough to land a plane on ...that's a yellow flag worth a second look. Not proof of a ghost job. Sometimes it's an honest mistake, an outdated template or a role that's still being scoped. But it's a fair question to ask before you pour an evening into a cover letter. Easy move: ask the recruiter what the realistic range is for the level they're hiring. A clear answer is a good sign. Sugar Glider grades every role against your resume so you can spend your energy on the ones worth it. Free beta at [link hidden] What's the widest pay range you've ever seen on a posting? #JobSearch #PayTransparency #BCJobs #CareerAdvice … more",
