      "url": null,
      "text": "You've found a job that looks perfect. Right skills, interesting company, good location and then you get to the salary... \"Competitive.\" Competitive with what? Recent research suggests that 41% of UK jobseekers wouldn't even apply for a vacancy without salary information. I can understand why some employers prefer not to advertise salaries, but are they potentially losing good candidates before they've even had a conversation? In this week's Tech Hiring Brief I've looked at both sides of the argument and whether salary transparency could actually make recruitment easier. Interested to hear what others think. Would you apply for a job without knowing the salary? … more",
