      "text": "PeopleTech Ltd. has five employees, earning €30,000, €40,000, €40,000, €50,000 and €100,000. The mean salary is €52,000. The median is €40,000. Neither is wrong. So why does the EU Pay Transparency Directive ask you to report both your mean and median gender pay gap? Because each one shows something different about where in your organisation a gap shows up. In this blog, we break down how they work and what your numbers might be telling you. … more",
