      "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7522115404895256576/",
      "text": "Dear LinkedIn, it's 2026. Isn't it high time we had a visa sponsorship filter? We can filter jobs by location, salary, experience, and work mode. But not by whether a company is open to sponsoring international candidates? As an international job seeker, imagine spending hours finding the perfect role, tailoring your resume, and filling out an application, only to reach the dreaded question Will you now or in the future require visa sponsorship? And just like that, your excitement turns into uncertainty. Here's what I find interesting: Employers can screen candidates based on sponsorship requirements. Why can't candidates filter employers by the same criteria? This isn't about asking companies to sponsor more people. It's about transparency, saving everyone's time, and making the job search a little less exhausting. A small feature. A massive difference. #LinkedIn #JobSearch #VisaSponsorship #InternationalStudents … more",
