      "url": null,
      "text": "In my last article I asked why poverty fell in Timor-Leste and admitted I did not know. A reader pushed me to look at the politics rather than the economics, so I went back through the state budget, a World Bank study I worked on, and my own focus groups. What I found: our domestic revenue covers about one-eighth of what the state spends, and our salary bill alone is now bigger than everything the Petroleum Fund can sustainably provide. The oil was not only paying for development. It was paying for our politics — the settlements, the jobs, the contracts that kept the peace after 2006. Both bills now fall due together. And the generation that will carry them told us last year, in six locations, that they cannot get into the room. In September they stood outside it instead. #TimorLeste #Youth #Governance #PublicFinance #Transparency #Leadership … more",
