      "url": null,
      "text": "Canva’s recent workforce restructuring, impacting 22% of its workforce, is difficult news. However, the support being offered to affected employees deserves appreciation. 👏 Here's what Canva is offering: 💰 6 months of salary 💻 Employees can keep their company laptops 🏥 Up to 12 months of healthcare coverage 📈 Removal of the one-year equity vesting cliff 🤝 Career coaching and job search assistance 🔗 1 year of LinkedIn Premium 🚀 $10,000 grants to start a business or community project, without taking any equity This is meaningful support during an uncertain time. But the bigger concern is that layoffs are becoming increasingly common across companies of all sizes, from small and mid-sized businesses to large MNCs. Lack of projects often becomes a reason to keep employees on the bench for 1–2 months, eventually leading to layoffs, with very little effort towards internal opportunities or project allocation. I've seen how deeply this affects people. During my time at Infinite, some of my teammates were impacted, and the uncertainty affected the entire team's morale. Business challenges are understandable, but employees deserve transparency, dignity and genuine support, especially during difficult times. Hope no one has to go through this phase. 🙏 … more",
