      "text": "Though outside my field and country, this post caught my attention. A compelling company I have watched expand seeks to fill a role—what exactly do they do? They publish an engaging ad, display the salary in matching font and a striking color, and thereby achieve 150% transparency. I can picture a boardroom where the salary idea arose: many eyebrows rose, some arguing that no one in the industry, sector, trade, country, or economy does this, while others suggested offering a range might be unnecessary since they could hire the desired person at slightly more than current pay and save money. Yet in my mind, someone said we act according to what is right for our people and culture, not what others expect or demand. Kudos to the Crumble team for this, even those who “might” have raised an eyebrow. … more",
