      "id": "LI01058",
      "sourceId": "LI01058",
      "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7523942537921953792/",
      "text": "Recruiter: “Hi, we have an exciting opportunity for you.” 👀 Candidate: “Great! Which company?” Recruiter: “It’s a confidential requirement.” Candidate: “Okay. What’s the job role?” Recruiter: “We’ll discuss that during the interview.” Candidate: “Can you at least share the salary range?” Recruiter: “It’s as per industry standards.” Candidate: “And the location?” Recruiter: “We’ll share the details once you’re shortlisted.” Candidate: “So what exactly should I prepare for?” Recruiter: “Just come with an open mind.” 💀 Candidate: “Should I bring my resume or a crystal ball?” 😂 Jokes apart, confidentiality is sometimes necessary in recruitment. But candidates shouldn’t have to attend an interview without knowing the basic details of the opportunity. A little transparency can save time for everyone. Recruiters, how much information should be shared with candidates before scheduling an interview? A) Company, role, salary and location B) Role and salary are enough C) Details can be shared during the interview #Recruitment #HR #Hiring #TalentAcquisition #CandidateExperience … more",
