      "text": "As a veteran in the #jobmarket I was always very verbal about unbiased recruitment and transparency in the hiring process. As per the new #equalpay Law in Greece, employers have to state the salary of a job opening upfront (either in the job posting or at least in the first interview). Also, gender mentions are not allowed in the job openings and definitely not in the hiring process. So no more \"I want a good looking blonde for my hotel reception\" and a \"nerdy guy for my IT department\". And of course this will come with bumps on the road and issues to be addressed down the road. But its a great step towards a transparent and fair recruitment process. [link hidden] … more",
