      "text": "Permanent Agile Delivery Manager 100% Remote Salary is DOE, which I know you don't want to hear, but there's method in my madness; we can discuss that privately. I'm working on an opportunity that will be good for someone who has moved beyond traditional Scrum Master responsibilities and wants to make a genuine impact on technology delivery. I need someone to take ownership of delivery across a major Clio Operate transformation within a leading law firm. This isn't a role where your success is measured by how many ceremonies you've facilitated. It's about: - Taking genuine accountability for Sprint, PI and wider delivery commitments. - Driving blockers, risks and dependencies through to resolution. - Constructively challenging teams and stakeholders when delivery isn't progressing. - Bringing clarity, transparency and confidence to delivery. - Improving SAFe, PI Planning and Agile ways of working. - Helping shape a wider Agile Centre of Excellence. The immediate focus is hands-on delivery across Clio Operate, supporting the migration of business capabilities from legacy systems onto the platform. The longer-term opportunity is equally interesting: the chance to develop into a broader delivery leadership position, with genuine succession planning towards Head of Delivery. If you're an experienced Agile Delivery Manager or Senior Scrum Master who enjoys taking ownership, solving problems and making things happen, I'd be keen to have a conversation. Equally, if someone in your network fits this profile, I'd really appreciate an introduction. Feel free to message me directly for a confidential discussion. … more",
