      "id": "LI01066",
      "sourceId": "LI01066",
      "url": null,
      "text": "🚨 Is Flutter Development Really Worth It in India Anymore? 🇮🇳 We spend years learning programming, building applications, fixing bugs, integrating APIs, handling deadlines, and constantly upgrading our technical skills. But are we getting paid fairly for our work? 💰 Let's compare some monthly earnings: ⛽ Petrol Pump Employee – ₹17,000 📦 Ekart Delivery Partner – Up to ₹40,000 💻 Flutter Developer – ₹20,000 These are illustrative figures. Actual earnings vary by location, experience, employer, incentives, and working hours. I'm not saying petrol pump employees or delivery partners deserve less. Every profession deserves respect and fair compensation. ❤️ But here's my question: Why are some skilled software developers still earning just ₹15,000–₹20,000 per month, even after gaining professional experience? Companies expect developers to: ✅ Build Android and iOS applications ✅ Integrate APIs and manage databases ✅ Fix production bugs ✅ Handle Play Store and App Store releases ✅ Learn new technologies continuously ✅ Deliver projects within tight deadlines Yet some companies hesitate to offer salaries that reflect these responsibilities. 📢 Let's Talk About Salary Transparency! I invite Flutter developers across India to share: 🏢 Company Name: 💻 Experience: 💰 Current Monthly Salary (₹): 📍 Location: Sharing company names is optional. Please share only what you're comfortable making public. Let's understand what Flutter developers are actually earning and encourage fair compensation across the industry. We are not asking for luxury. We are asking for fair pay for our skills, experience, and contributions. What's your opinion? Is Flutter development undervalued in India? #Flutter #FlutterDeveloper #SalaryTransparency #FairPay #SoftwareDeveloper #ITJobs #TechIndustry #India #DeveloperCommunity #CareerGrowth … more",
      "jobFamily": "工程与技术",
