      "text": "A company can have the biggest recruiting budget in the world. But if their hiring experience is terrible, top talent will walk away. Things that are IN: ✅ NO ghosting ✅ Pay transparency ✅ Giving people a chance ✅ Respecting candidates' time ✅ Faster, more efficient hiring processes ✅ Timely communication throughout the process ✅ Providing interview feedback whenever possible Things that are OUT: ⛔ Ageism in hiring ⛔ Ghosting candidates ⛔ Asking for salary history ⛔ One-way video interviews ⛔ Multi-month interview processes ⛔ Job descriptions with unrealistic \"wish lists\" ⛔ Unpaid assignments that require hours of work The hiring process says everything about a company's culture. Treat candidates with respect. Communicate. Value their time. That's how you build a reputation that attracts great talent. ▶️ What would you add to each list? … more",
