      "id": "LI01076",
      "sourceId": "LI01076",
      "url": null,
      "text": "💼 PAYROLL SERIES – DAY 5: UNDERSTANDING PAYROLL DEDUCTIONS Do you know how much of an employee's gross salary is deducted before they receive their net pay? Payroll deductions are an important part of salary processing. Every HR professional should understand what is deducted, why it is deducted, and how it is calculated. 📌 Types of Payroll Deductions: 1️⃣ Statutory Deductions - Income Tax (as applicable) - Provident Fund (PF) - ESI (where applicable) 2️⃣ Employee Benefits - Health Insurance - Group Life Insurance - Other voluntary benefits 3️⃣ Loan Deductions - Personal Loans - Salary Advances - Housing Loans (if applicable) 4️⃣ Other Deductions - Absence or unpaid leave adjustments - Other authorized deductions as per company policy 🎯 Why Are Accurate Deductions Important? ✅ Ensure legal and policy compliance. ✅ Maintain payroll accuracy. ✅ Build employee trust. ✅ Promote transparency. ✅ Avoid salary-related disputes. 💡 Remember: Gross Salary – Applicable Deductions = Net Salary. As HR professionals, our responsibility is not just to process salaries but also to ensure accuracy, transparency, and employee satisfaction. Let's discuss! 👇 Which payroll deduction do you find most challenging to manage in your organization? #PayrollManagement #HumanResources #HRProfessional #PayrollProcessing #SalaryManagement #HRLearning #AyeshaLodhi … more",
