      "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:share:7528321086137057283/",
      "text": "We're Hiring | Product Manager – Mint (Digital) #Hiring, I'm looking for a Product Manager who doesn't just manage roadmaps but knows how to build products that consumers love, use and keep coming back to. -- What we're looking for: 5–7 years in B2C products , ideally someone who has built or scaled consumer-facing digital products. AI-native mindset , uses AI to prototype, experiment, automate and ship faster. Not just to write PRDs. Consumer obsession , understands why users form habits, what makes them return and why they eventually stop. Growth + Product thinking , knows how to move DAU, retention, engagement and monetisation, not just ship features. Data fluency , comfortable with SQL, funnels, cohorts, experimentation and making decisions backed by data. Builder mentality , can turn an idea into a working product without waiting for a 20-page requirements document. Commercial instinct , understands that great products must eventually deliver great business outcomes. -- Location: Delhi/NCR, Work from Office | 5 Days a Week Now, here's the interesting part. Before you send your CV, here's a small challenge. Imagine you're Mint's Product Manager and you've been given one mission: Make Mint an app people (Affluent) open every morning , before Instagram, WhatsApp or even their morning coffee. You have 30 days, a small engineering team and ZERO additional marketing budget. What's your first move? -- No generic AI features. No loyalty points. No \"let's send more notifications.\"Tell me what you'd build, why users would care and what number would convince you it's working. 200 words max. Bonus points if you can show a quick AI-built prototype. I'm interested in how you think, not how well you write a PRD. If this sounds like you, DM me or Sameeksha Chauhan your CV and your response to the challenge.",
