      "text": "🔎 JD X-RAY #101: 🚨 PRIME VIDEO IS HIRING A SENIOR PRODUCT MANAGER. I read the JD. [[link hidden]] ➡️ India roadmap. ➡️ Emerging markets. ➡️ Payments. ➡️ Subscriptions. ➡️ Personalisation. ➡️ App experience. ➡️ Local pricing. ➡️ Partner bundles. ➡️ Content discovery. At this point, are you hiring a Product Manager… OR THE PERSON WHO FINDS THE REMOTE FOR THE ENTIRE STREAMING BUSINESS? 😂 Imagine the interview: Interviewer: “What will you own?” Candidate: “India's customer experience.” Interviewer: “Great. Now align with four worldwide product teams.” Candidate: “Should I bring popcorn or a diplomatic passport?” 🤣 Here's your PM X-RAY exercise: Before applying, decode: 1. Which market decisions do YOU own? 2. Which global platform decisions can you influence? 3. Which customer and commercial metrics define success? Because local ownership with global dependencies is a very different job from owning the entire product stack. PMs: What's the funniest example you've seen of a role having ownership without enough decision rights? I suspect this comment section needs its own season on Prime Video. 😂 #ProductManagement #ProductJobs #PrimeVideo #ProductLeadership #CareerStrategy #JDXRay #HiringPanelLens",
