      "text": "Leading with \"know what makes a great video hook\" is exactly right — for social-first content, the hook does more work than the other 59 seconds combined. Cutting 15+ videos a month as a senior editor, I've seen the first 3 seconds decide retention more than any transition ever could. Curious: with Forbes' pace, do hooks get tested as variations before a video ships, or is it more instinct-led in the edit? … more",
